femto patch for epub-stream 0.1.0
Subject: collect linked and embedded chapter CSS in order, with shared limits

Upstream collects only <link rel="stylesheet"> hrefs, ignores <style>
elements, applies max_css_bytes per stylesheet and max_selectors per
stylesheet, and silently stops on XML errors.

- parse_chapter_style_sources replaces parse_stylesheet_links[_bytes]. It
  returns linked and embedded sources in document order, decodes CDATA and
  XML references in <style>, honours type (text/css) and media (all/screen),
  caps sources at 256 and embedded bytes at the CSS limit, and reports XML
  errors.
- max_css_bytes and max_selectors become chapter-wide totals. Styler tracks
  accumulated bytes and rules; linked stylesheets are read with the remaining
  byte budget as a hard cap; css::parse_stylesheet_bounded stops before
  retaining an excess rule.
- A failed load clears the partially built cascade and the counters.
- EpubBook::chapter_stylesheets_with_options and the scratch-buffer variant
  use the same collector and budget.

femto needs embedded <style> support for real books and bounded total CSS
memory per chapter on the device.

